# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environment
#
# NOTE: this project has its own top-level Lib/ and Scripts/ directories that
# hold source code. A virtualenv also contains Lib/ and Scripts/, so NEVER add
# bare "Lib/" or "Scripts/" patterns here - they would silently exclude the
# entire codebase. Exclude the venv by its own directory name only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode / build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / IDE
#
# .vscode/settings.json IS tracked on purpose: it points Pylance at Lib/ so
# imports resolve, and selects the .venv interpreter. Without it every script
# shows false "could not be resolved" warnings.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS clutter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment output
#
# benchmark_results.csv, slip_results.csv and benchmark_report/ are
# deliberately NOT ignored. The CSVs hold measurements that cannot be
# regenerated without repeating the whole experiment, and the report is the
# deliverable built from them. Both belong in version control.
#
# Config/gripper_limits.yaml is generated by the calibration wizard but is also
# tracked on purpose: it records which set of fingers the committed results
# were taken with.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
